      ],
      "selected_passed_stage_a": true
    },
    "rationale": "Multi-metric selection under the preregistered ordered screen; no single metric decided, and DA floors degraded to the RankIC t-stat health gate (all arms hug coin-flip DA, as expected). (1) Signal: 64x192 has the strongest late RankIC of the sweep, 0.0418 (t=7.35), vs 0.0364 (48x256), 0.0339 (128x384), and only 0.0238 (t=3.42) for 96x192 - i.e. 64x192 leads the runner-up by 15% and the behaviour-best 96x192 by 76%. (2) Information: joint MI 1.34 bits/token is top-tier (vs 1.28 for 96x192), so it lets the GPT extract the most learnable signal. (3) Capacity-normalized behaviour: 64x192 is first on collapse alignment (0.429) and second on distribution alignment (0.454) and balance-p10, i.e. first-tier with no weak axis; 96x192 edges it on distribution/unique alignment but only by sacrificing 43% of downstream RankIC - a mid-pipeline alignment gain that fails to convert into signal, so it is not selected. (4) Amplitude AmpRatio 1.22 is near 1 and stable. Tokenizer MAE 0.218 is mid-pack and, per the non-transmission principle, played no selection role. Note 64x192 is the default tokenizer architecture used in Exp 01, so the sweep confirms rather than overturns the default: no larger encoder improves downstream signal.",
